pes-dashed","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Patience starting to run thin for head coaches in Week 11","description":"Saturday didn't offer much to change the season's complexion, but some coaches are coming under pressure.","published":"2026-11-15T06:25:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedayfinal111426/week-11-top-games-highlights-takeaways","type":"Story","byline":"Kyle Bonagura","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Arch Manning leads game-winning drive as Texas stuns LSU","description":"Arch Manning found Raleek Brown for a 4-yard touchdown pass along the left sideline with 3 seconds left, and Texas escaped Tiger Stadium with a victory over LSU on Saturday night.","published":"2026-11-15T06:28:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50487515/arch-manning-leads-game-winning-drive-texas-stuns-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest's post-blowout jab at SMU tops college football Week 11 trolls","description":"Wake Forest dominated SMU on the gridiron Saturday -- and added insult to injury after the game.","published":"2026-11-15T05:30:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481104/college-football-trolls-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who are the winningest college football coaches of all time?","description":"From Saban to Paterno, there are many legendary college football coaches. Who has the best career record? Check out who has the most wins now.","published":"2026-11-15T04:25:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/39283806/who-winningest-college-football-coaches-all","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Louisville holds off UNC in game that ends with brawl","description":"Louisville held off North Carolina 16-14 on Saturday night in a game that ended in a brawl and each of the teams having to be separated.","published":"2026-11-15T04:55:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50486992/louisville-holds-unc-game-ends-brawl","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Kentucky's CFP hopes take hit in upset loss to Gators, Philo","description":"Florida quarterback Aaron Philo had 221 all-purpose yards and a touchdown to rally the Gators past No. 11 Kentucky 21-14 Saturday.","published":"2026-11-15T04:13:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50486400/kentucky-cfp-hopes-take-hit-upset-loss-gators-philo","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No. 24 Boise State outlasts Oregon State, to host Pac-12 title game","description":"Rasean Jones caught 11 passes for 230 yards and 3 TDs to help No. 24 Boise State outlast Oregon State 46-41 and wrap up the host spot in the Pac-12 title game.","published":"2026-11-15T03:30:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50486399/boise-state-outlasts-oregon-state-host-pac-12-title-game","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No. 16 Oregon keeps CFP hopes alive with win over Michigan","description":"Dylan Raiola threw for 341 yards and four touchdowns, and No. 16 Oregon kept its slim chances for a spot in the College Football Playoff alive with a victory over struggling Michigan on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-15T03:15:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50485510/no16-oregon-keeps-cfp-hopes-alive-win-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Grant Wilson delivers as Indiana boosts CFP, Big Ten hopes with win vs. USC","description":"With Grant Wilson filling in at quarterback, No. 9 Indiana ramped up its offensive attack against USC and scored its best win of the season Saturday.","published":"2026-11-15T03:22:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50485076/grant-wilson-indiana-boost-cfp-big-ten-hopes-win-vs-usc","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4685314/sebastian-cheeks","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastian_Cheeks"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Sebastian Cheeks","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastian_Cheeks","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:20Z","intro":"Sebastian Cheeks (born February 6, 2004) is an American college football outside linebacker for the Wisconsin Badgers. He previously played for the North Carolina Tar Heels.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Cheeks attended Evanston Township High School in Evanston, Illinois, where he played linebacker and running back. As a sophomore he recorded two interceptions which he returned for touchdowns over his first four games before suffering a season-ending injury. Cheeks was selected to play in the 2022 All-American Bowl, where he was named the All-American Bowl's Man of the Year. A four-star recruit, he committed to University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Cheeks played the 2022 and 2023 season with North Carolina, recording four tackles over eight games. After the 2023 season, he entered the transfer portal and committed to the University of Wisconsin Madison. In his first year at Wisconsin in 2024, he played in 11 games and had 12 tackles with two sacks. Cheeks started three of 12 games in 2025, recording 24 tackles and three sacks. He returned to Wisconsin as a starter in 2026."}]}}